the horizontal axis when overflowing it goes to next line and on vertical axis, have a way to \"scroll\" the text in order to see the rest of it (maybe with a scroll bar, maybe with an input) like we can do in CSS with the overflow: auto, or overflow: scroll property\r\n\r\ni just tried it with bevy 0.11 and it seems to work on the horizontal axis with the linebreak_behavior field on the Text type, on the vertical axis though, i don't know how to make it works, i can clip it yes, but how to retrieve the rest of the text then ? Is there currently a way to know wich part of the text is not visible ? Or to \"scroll\" it ?\r\n\r\nShould i close this issue ? Even if it's not quite what i wanted, there is now a fix to the overflowing problem","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/1640477077/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"Azales94500","id":52787987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNzg3OTg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52787987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Azales94500","html_url":"https://github.com/Azales94500","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Azales94500/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Azales94500/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Azales94500/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Azales94500/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Azales94500/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Azales94500/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Azales94500/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Azales94500/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Azales94500/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":fals